{"Title":"An Act relative to selling tattooing, branding, body piercing kit or device to an unlicensed body art practitioner or minor","BillNumber":"H1386","DocketNumber":"HD1090","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"BJA1","Name":"Bruce J. Ayers","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/BJA1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-18T10:56:54.04"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"BJA1","Name":"Bruce J. Ayers","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/BJA1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-18T10:56:54.04"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H1386/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Representative Ayers of Quincy, a petition (accompanied by bill, House, No. 1386) of Bruce J. Ayers for legislation to establish a penalty for the sale of tattooing, branding or body piercing devices to unlicensed body art practitioners or minors.  The Judiciary.","DocumentText":"\tSECTION 1. Chapter 111 of the General Laws is hereby amended by adding the following section:-\r\n\t230. Whoever gives or sells a tattooing, branding, or body piercing kit or other tattooing, branding, or body piercing device to an unlicensed body art practitioner or a minor shall be subject to a fine of not more than $500.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J19","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J19"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}